# Vault .gitignore — ships with the template; governs YOUR vault repo.

# Vault-local Python environment (see config.env / USING-THIS-TEMPLATE.md)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Generated refine queue (rewritten by vault-refine-detect.py)
20-Claims/_refine-queue.json

# Obsidian per-machine UI state (keep the rest of .obsidian tracked)
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache

.DS_Store

# Private live config — framework ships config.defaults.env + config.env.example; create yours via `cp` (ADR-0020)
99-Operations/config.env

# Rendered Layer-0 fleet. Generated output; its SOURCE is 99-Operations/scripts/*.md and
# `render` recreates it. Tracking it would give one piece of code two homes - the note and a
# committed copy - which is the duplication the literate meta-script model exists to prevent
# (INV-3), and would make every render a diff to review.
# NOTE the narrowness: this ignores the generated output DIRECTORY only, never a parent that
# also holds tracked scaffold. A blanket rule silently hides the next artifact deployed beneath it.
99-Operations/bin/
